//! The Simplicity program an accumulator batch's exit spends by, pruned, as
//! sequentia-contracts publishes it: `templates/arca_accumulator/exits.json`
//! (`arca/accumulator-1`). The pruned program is one of two constants,
//! whatever the batch, the slot, the input index or the key that signs, so an
//! exit is built with no compiler. Copied byte for byte; the regtest tests
//! spend both on the node.

/// The commitment root of `arca/accumulator-1`.
pub const ACCUMULATOR_CMR: &str = "9b6467a1f9d787f6e93ac2422194e61fc56638db63735c6f24ba2c7a86bc0b96";

/// `arca/accumulator-1`, an exit that leaves a rest (2003 bytes).
pub const ACCUMULATOR_EXIT: &str = "";

/// `arca/accumulator-1`, an exit that takes the last of the batch (1877 bytes).
pub const ACCUMULATOR_EXIT_LAST: &str = "";
